## Abstract
The development of high latitude continental margin has been mainly controlled by glacigenic processes during the glacial maxima. Superimposed to these, there are both downslope and alongslope sedimentary processes (turbidites and contourites). This study is part of a PhD project, aiming to study the relationships between the glacial sedimentary input and the water circulation in NW Barents Sea (Kveithola to Isfjorden Trough Mouth Fans). This portion of the Barents Sea has been the target of several surveys in the last decade: SVAIS (R/V Hesperides) in 2007, EGLACOM (R/V OGS Explora) in 2008, GLACIBAR (R/V Jan Mayen) in 2009,
